<title>FRANCE: Kurds ask Turkish pullout from Iraq.</title>
<headline>Kurds ask Turkish pullout from Iraq.</headline>
<dateline>STRASBOURG, France 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some 30 Kurdish intellectuals demanding the pullout of Turkish forces from northern Iraq protested outside the European Parliament on Tuesday and asked that the European Union halt aid to Ankara.</p>
<p>The protesters chained themselves to flagpoles outside the parliament's headquarters in the eastern French city of Strasbourg.</p>
<p>In a letter to the parliamentarians, they urged the EU to take a strong stand on the three-week-old Turkish push into Iraq and asked to meet a member of the European Commission.</p>
<p>Thousands of Turkish troops, backed by air power, have been in Kurdish-held areas of Iraq since May 14 in a cross-border operation against Kurdistan Workers Party (PKK) bases used for raids into southeast Turkey.</p>
</text>
